        "v": [
          "#### Repositories that could not be checked",
          "These repositories are linked in the paper, but their contents could not be retrieved, so nothing below describes them. When the reason is that the platform did not answer, running the check again later may work.",
          "- https://osf.io/parc2: closed registration source",
          "#### Whose Deposits",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Repository = \"<a href='https://osf.io/regc2' target='_blank'>osf.io/regc2<\/a>\", \n    \"Cited in\" = \"text\", Whose = \"the authors', for this paper\", \n    Why = \"a link in the main text, not shown to be anyone else's\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### Repositories",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Repository = \"<a href='https://osf.io/parc2' target='_blank'>osf.io/parc2<\/a>\", \n    Platform = \"osf\", Error = \"closed registration source\", \"All Files\" = 0L, \n    \"Data Files\" = 0L, \"Code Files\" = 0L, READMEs = 0L, Archives = 0L), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = c(\"tbl_df\", \"tbl\", \"data.frame\"))\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "",
          "README files were found in all repositories.",
          "#### Registration Points to a Closed Project\n\n1 OSF project (https://osf.io/parc2) is referenced by a registration in this manuscript, but it is closed or inaccessible, and no copy of its files could be found anywhere else. Some OSF registrations only describe what was shared, while the actual files live in the project they were registered from — if that project is closed and the registration holds no copy, metacheck cannot list or download its files, and other researchers cannot access them either. Consider making the source project openly available, or re-uploading its files directly into the registration."
